<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary operations.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary operations.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all three direct sales of paper and four repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 2.777 billion pesos from the secondary market on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    353 days   20.79 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    178 days   20.69 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     87 days   19.61 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    800 million     38 days   20.29 pct</p>
<p>    750 million     31 days   19.58 pct</p>
<p>    600 million	9 days   19.99 pct</p>
<p>    177 million	1 day    19.49 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
